{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And if you offer a meal-offering of first fruits.</b> Many say that the word אם is an obligation. In my opinion there is no need, for the obligation is ראשית בכורים, and not הבכורים. And whoever wishes to bring a meal-offering of first fruits as a freewill offering, he may bring." "<b>Aviv.</b> It is called thus because it is first, and it is from the root אב." "<b>Geres.</b> Its meaning is known and close to the root of גרסה נפשי, and if it is with samekh." "<b>Carmel.</b> Like וכרמל בצקלונו."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:32.483007945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}